{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Parent epic 1386 was remediated — read before implementing\n\nThe epic's AC1 was UNSATISFIABLE as written (it banned all SC vocabulary under `src/rebar/`\nwhile its own Scope deferred some) and has been amended. This does not change your scope, but\nit fixes what \"done\" means for the epic, and it names carve-outs you must NOT \"fix\":\n\n**Four permanent vocabulary carve-outs** — leave these exactly as they are:\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T2.md` — \"a pilot with metrics, or stated success\n  criteria for a trial\". Generic English about an EXPERIMENT succeeding, not the ticket\n  heading. Story 2aa6's AC6 REQUIRES it to survive.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md`,\n  `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md`, and the `dod_uncertifiable` field\n  description in `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py` — the\n  `dod_uncertifiable` / \"definition-of-done\" concept, which this epic explicitly defers.\n\n**Also amended:** epic AC5 now pins `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` at EXACTLY ONE SC\nmatch (T2's echo) rather than zero — the guide is GENERATED from the criteria registry and\nembeds each criterion's prompt verbatim, so zero was impossible.\n\n**A gap was found and assigned to 5f4d, not to you:** `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:288`\n(\"its success criteria are met across children\") is genuine heading-sense vocabulary that no\nstory owned. It is now in 5f4d's scope. Don't pick it up here.\n\nPattern worth knowing before you write your own checks: four acceptance criteria in this epic\nso far (35bc AC1/AC3, 2aa6 AC1/AC3) were blanket string prohibitions that collided with their\nown deliberate exclusions, each needing a mid-implementation amendment and a re-review. If\nyour AC contains an absolute \"returns no matches\", check it against the exclusions first."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785018747323398001,"uuid":"b9f96cf3-d58a-4695-9a8f-26d0c9ed576b"}